HUMAN-APPLY STEP - COMPLETE, and the evidence is this round's own measurement.
 - tasks.md T-012's "Human apply step (separate, explicit - required before Done)" and its Done
   When item "The Human apply step above is complete and recorded in the implementation report"
   are satisfied by commit c50f2c64, "feat(epic-189-a1): apply the staged ADR-0023 track-selection
   migration to the protected consumers (T-012)". `git log --oneline -1 --` against each protected
   live path returns c50f2c64 for BOTH, so that commit and no other carries the applied bytes.
 - The apply was performed BY A HUMAN through the now-protected `apply-human-copy`, as TWO
   SINGLE-TARGET BATCHES. A single two-target batch is not merely undesirable but IMPOSSIBLE, and
   that was demonstrated empirically this round rather than argued from the spec. Both targets'
   basename is literally `SKILL.md`, and the publisher refuses a same-basename batch at
   manifest-parse time, before any live mutation (plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/apply-human-
   copy.sh:570-578, with EXIT_DUPLICATE_BASENAME_IN_BATCH=19 defined at :102). Driven against an
   isolated `git clone --local` of HEAD in a throwaway directory outside the repository, with a
   hand-written two-entry manifest naming both protected paths:

     {"status":"denied","category":"DUPLICATE_BASENAME_IN_BATCH","message":"manifest target
      'plugins/sdd-lite/skills/lite-spec/SKILL.md' shares basename 'SKILL.md' (compared
      case-insensitively) with an earlier target in the same batch; the pre-transaction backup
      path is basename-keyed (design.md:1011) and cannot safely hold two colliding targets in one
      transaction"}
     publisher-exit=19

   `git status --porcelain` in that clone is EMPTY afterwards, confirming the refusal preceded any
   mutation; the real worktree was never the target and is likewise clean. This is round 1's Major
   finding, and it is why the runbook prescribes two batches.
 - POST-APPLY LIVE DIGESTS, measured with `shasum -a 256` against the live files at HEAD:

     0761a91547375da3456a5aa60d220543f3831d2e1986086f10a70a037bd6d5c9  plugins/sdd-ship/skills/ship/SKILL.md
     757c681731aa766bf95ec016fc0f4a39216feb00a9ecca71f8b70a94cb1a9679  plugins/sdd-lite/skills/lite-spec/SKILL.md

   These EQUAL the staged candidates' digests exactly - the same two values come back from
   `shasum -a 256` over specs/epic-189-a1-project-context/human-copy/plugins/sdd-ship/skills/
   ship/SKILL.md and .../sdd-lite/skills/lite-spec/SKILL.md. Equality of digests was then
   strengthened to byte equality: `cmp` over each live/staged pair exits 0. The apply is exact,
   not merely approximately faithful.
 - PRE-APPLY LIVE DIGESTS, read out of git rather than remembered: `git show 856c514f:<path> |
   shasum -a 256` gives 5748a0928443bc63307bf3ab7bdb75c158bdfbef9cde72e3b3f5354bac063e91 for ship
   and 40fdba6f1849effb06a8439a09b92a192a36b42a708c3cf1a253d7d48a50fc74 for lite-spec. Those are
   the two values the seq0371 report independently reconstructed by reverse-applying each
   persisted diff onto the staged candidate, so the pre-state, the delta and the post-state now
   agree from three directions.
 - MANIFEST agreement: `shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256` run from
   specs/epic-189-a1-project-context/human-copy/ reports OK for all TEN entries, exit 0, including
   entry 9 (ship, 0761a915…) and entry 10 (lite-spec, 757c6817…). The manifest, the staged bytes
   and the live bytes are one consistent set.
 - TEST-PUB, the suite's own view of the apply, now reports `published` for both consumers, `no
   staged/live drift` for both, and its pair-consistency assertion green. Its state-classifying
